{"id":"word:hebrew:H3881","type":"word","title":"לֵוִיִּי","subtitle":"H3881 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"a Levite or descendant of Levi","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to לֵוִיִּי (H3881) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: a.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 286 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"לֵוִיִּי (Lêvîyîy) means a Levite or descendant of Levi First listed occurrence: 1Chr 6 4."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"לֵוִיִּי","transliteration":"Lêvîyîy","pronunciation":"lay-vee-ee'","strong":"H3881","lemmaId":"hebrew:H3881","partOfSpeech":"a","forms":["הַ/לְוִיִּ֔ם","הַ/לְוִיִּ֖ם","הַ/לְוִיִּ֑ם","הַ/לְוִיִּֽם","הַ/לְוִיִּ֗ם"],"morphs":[["HTd/Ngmpa",147],["HC/Td/Ngmpa",58],["HRd/Ngmpa",35],["HTd/Ngmsa",21],["HC/Rd/Ngmpa",9],["HC/Td/Ngmsa",6],["HNgmsa",3],["HNp",2],["HRd/Ngmsa",2],["HR/Np",1]]},"definitions":{"short":"a Levite or descendant of Levi","usage":"Leviite.","full":"H3881. Leviyyi or Levi II. לֵוִי 291 adjective, of a people Levite ; — לֵוִי , 40 t.; plural לֵוִיִּם 250t.; suffix לְוִיֵּנוּ Neh 10:1 ; &#8212; l. singular of individual, ל ׳אִישׁ Judg 19:1 a certain Levite ; predicate ל ׳וְהוּא 17:1 and he was a Levite , so 17:9 ; with article ׳הַלּ as substantive the Levite Exod 4:11 (J), Judg 17:10-11 , 12 , 13 (as priest), Deut 18:6 ; 2Chr 20:14 ; 31:12 , 14 ; Ezra 10:15 ; הַלּ ׳הַנַּעַר Judg 18:3 , 15 ; הַלּ ׳הָאִישׁ 20:4 . Sg. usually 2 with article הַלֵּוִי as substantive collective the Levites: Exod 6:19 ; Num 3:20 , 32 ; 26:57 (all P); 18:23 (P; charged with service of tabernacle); especially D, Deut 12:12 , 18 , 19 ; 14:27 , 29 ; 16:1 , 14 ; 26:10 , 12 , 13 ; also 1Chr 24:6 ; Mal 2:8 (as priestly tribe); הַלּ ׳שֵׁבָט Deut 10:8 tribe of the Levites (set apart for service), compare Josh 13:14 , 33 ; 1Chr 23:14 ; בְּנֵיהַֿלֵּוִי 12:27 (van d. H v. 12:26 ) sons of the Levites (i.e. of the tribe); so Nehemiah 10:40 (as tithe-collectors); הַלֵּוִי בֵּית Psa 135:20 house (family, tribe) of the Levites. 3 plural לְוִיִּם chiefly Chronicles and P; — always with article ַהלְוִיִּם except suffix לוִיֵּנוּ Neh 10:1 ; the article is omitted by ᵑ9 ᵐ5 and most in Isa 66:21 ; always = substantive Levites ; — 1 a. earlier usage: — as bearing the ark 1Sam 6:15 ; 2Sam 15:24 ; Deut 31:25 , so (with priests) 1Kin 8:4 2Chr 5:5 (HCT הַל ׳הכהנים ; read probably ׳וְהַל as in Kings, ᵑ9 ᵑ6 ᵐ5 compare Öttli VB); also 1Chronicles is 1Chr 15:2 , 26 , 27 ; 23:26 ; 2Chr 5:4 (for הכהנים || 1Kin 8:3 ). b. not distinguished from priests by D: הַל ׳הַכֹּהֲנִים Deut 17:9 , 18 ; 18:1 ; 24:8 ; 27:9 ; Josh 3:3 ; 8:33 (both D; as bearing ark), also Jer 33:18 , 21 ׳(הַל ׳הַכ ׅ , Ezek 43:19 ; 44:15 ; compare Deut 18:7 ; 27:14 ; Jer 33:22 ; ׳הַכ ׳הַל likewise 2Chr 23:18 ; 30:27 (but read probably ׳וְהַל after ᵑ9 ᵑ6 ᵐ5 , compare Öttli and below) c. as tribal designation , Exod 6:25 ; Num 3:39 ; 4:18 , 46 ; Josh 21:1 (all P), 1Chr 9:33-34 , 15:12 ; 2Chr 35:5 ; Neh 11:15-16 , 12:24 ; with reference to share in land Lev 25:32 (twice in verse); 25:33 (twice in verse) (H), Num 1:47 ; 2:33 ; Josh 14:3-4 , 21:3-4 , 8 , 20 , 27 , 34 , 38 , 39 (all P), 18:7 (D), 1Chr 6:49 ; compare also 2Chr 11:14 . d. set apart for service in tabernacle , Exod 38:21 ; Num 1:50-51 , (twice in verse); 1:53 (twice in verse); 2:17 ; 7:5-6 , 8:6 18 t. Numbers 8 (all p), compare 1Chr 6:33 ; 16:4 ; ministers to Aaron and his sons Num 3:9 ; 8:19 ; 18:6 (P); set apart for ׳י (as redemption for first-born) 3:12 (twice in verse) + 7 t. Numbers 3 (P); with certain perquisites 18:24 , 26 , 30 9 t. Numbers (P). 2 in Chronicles the tribal idea is in the background, and thought of Levites as official class is prominent: a. distinguished from priests ׳הַכ ׳וְהַל 1Chr 9:14 (compare 9:10 ), 13:2 ; 15:4 , 11 , 14 ; 23:2 ; 24:6 , 31 67t. Chronicles; also Isa 66:21 (according to Vrss., but dubious), Ezek 44:10 ; 45:5 (compare 45:4 ), 48:11-12 , 13 , 22 . b. as porters , 1Chr 9:26 ; 26:17 , compare 1Chron 34:9; as in charge of music, 15:16-17 , 22 ; 2Chr 5:12 ; 29:25 , 30 ; 34:12 ; Neh 12:27 ; yet distinguished from porters and singers, 7:1 ; 13:5 , 10 ; distinguished also from נְתִינִים 1Chr 9:2 ; Ezra 8:20 ; Neh 10:29 ; further (with various official functions) 1Chr 9:31 29 t. Chronicles; of groups of individuals, 2Chr 17:8 (twice in verse); 29:12 ; 34:12 ; Ezra 2:40 = Neh 7:43 ; Ezra 8:33 ; Neh 3:17 ; 9:5 ; 10:10 ; 12:8 , also 8:7 (omitted וְ ; ᵑ9 BeRy Ryle). c. בְּנֵיהַֿלְוִיִּם 1Chr 15:15 (bearing ark), 24:30 (tribal designation). — See, on Levites, especially Gf Geschichte. d. Stammes Levi in Me Archiv i. 68 ff. 208 ff. We Prol. Cap. iv RS OTJC. 435 f., 2nd ed., 360 f. Bau Priesterthum 50 f. , 68 f., and often","rootNote":"or לֵוִי ; patronymically from 3878 ;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Chr 6 4","keyReferences":["1Chr 6 4","1Chr 6 33","1Chr 6 49","1Chr 9 2","1Chr 9 14","1Chr 9 26","1Chr 9 31","1Chr 9 33"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":286,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Chr 6 4","book":"1Chr","chapter":6,"verse":4,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"הַ/לֵּוִ֖י","source":"hebrew","morph":"HTd/Ngmsa"},{"reference":"1Chr 6 33","book":"1Chr","chapter":6,"verse":33,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"הַ/לְוִיִּ֑ם","source":"hebrew","morph":"HTd/Ngmpa"},{"reference":"1Chr 6 49","book":"1Chr","chapter":6,"verse":49,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"לַ/לְוִיִּ֑ם","source":"hebrew","morph":"HRd/Ngmpa"},{"reference":"1Chr 9 2","book":"1Chr","chapter":9,"verse":2,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"הַ/לְוִיִּ֖ם","source":"hebrew","morph":"HTd/Ngmpa"},{"reference":"1Chr 9 14","book":"1Chr","chapter":9,"verse":14,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"הַ/לְוִיִּ֑ם","source":"hebrew","morph":"HTd/Ngmpa"},{"reference":"1Chr 9 26","book":"1Chr","chapter":9,"verse":26,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"הַ/לְוִיִּ֑ם","source":"hebrew","morph":"HTd/Ngmpa"},{"